# Refactoring Dashboard Pages into Modular Component Folders

Refactor each dashboard page in `src/pages/` into its own directory containing the entry point (`index.tsx`) and separate files for individual subcomponents. This improves codebase readability, maintainability, and adheres to structured organization principles.

## User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> All page routes in `src/routes/index.tsx` will remain lazy-loaded using `React.lazy`. Because the entry point for each directory is `index.tsx`, the lazy import paths (e.g. `import('../pages/Dashboard')`) will automatically resolve without changing the filename, ensuring zero routing downtime.

## Proposed Changes

### Dashboard Component (`src/pages/Dashboard/`)
Create a new folder `src/pages/Dashboard/` and split `src/pages/Dashboard.tsx` into:
- [NEW] `src/pages/Dashboard/index.tsx` — Main dashboard layout.
- [NEW] `src/pages/Dashboard/WelcomeBanner.tsx` — Premium welcome banner card containing wallet balance.
- [NEW] `src/pages/Dashboard/MetricsGrid.tsx` — Overview metrics cards (portfolio value, stock holdings, etc.).
- [NEW] `src/pages/Dashboard/InvestmentPlans.tsx` — Featured investment plans section.
- [NEW] `src/pages/Dashboard/LedgerActivity.tsx` — Quick ledger activity and partner network referral links.
- [DELETE] `src/pages/Dashboard.tsx`

---

